## Why This Is Asked
This tests DP over partitions with a non-linear block cost dependent on average, plus reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- Partition DP over k blocks
- Prefix sums for O(1) block sums
- Non-linear, floor(sum/len) cost
- Backtracking for endpoints
- Time: O(n^2 k); Space: O(nk)

## Code Example
```javascript
function minCostPartition(A, k){
  const n = A.length;
  const pref = new Array(n+1).fill(0);
  for(let i=0;i<n;i++) pref[i+1] = pref[i] + A[i];
  const INF = 1e15;
  const dp = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=>Array(k+1).fill(INF));
  const par = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=>Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++){
    for(let t=1;t<=Math.min(i,k);t++){
      for(let p=t-1;p<=i-1;p++){
        const sum = pref[i]-pref[p];
        const len = i-p;
        const cost = Math.floor(sum/len);
        if(dp[p][t-1] + cost < dp[i][t]){
          dp[i][t] = dp[p][t-1] + cost;
          par[i][t] = p;
        }
      }
    }
  }
  let blocks = [], i=n, t=k;
  while(t>0){
    const p = par[i][t];
    blocks.push([p+1, i]);
    i = p; t--;
  }
  blocks.reverse();
  return {cost: dp[n][k], blocks};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How to optimize to faster than O(n^2 k)?
- How to handle negatives or alternative cost such as max/min?

## Why This Is Asked
This problem tests the ability to design a dynamic programming solution for array partitioning with a per-segment objective function. It combines partition DP with range maximum queries and reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- Dynamic programming over array partitions
- Range maximum queries (precomputation table M[a][b])
- Path reconstruction using parent pointers
- Time/space complexity: O(n²k) time, O(nk) space

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxPartition(A, k, c){
  const n = A.length-1; // 1-indexed array
  const M = Array.from({length:n+2}, ()=>Array(n+2).fill(0));

  // Precompute range maximums
  for(let i=1; i<=n; i++){
    M[i][i] = A[i];
    for(let j=i+1; j<=n; j++){
      M[i][j] = Math.max(M[i][j-1], A[j]);
    }
  }

  const dp = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=>Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const par = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=>Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;

  for(let t=1; t<=k; t++){
    for(let i=t; i<=n; i++){
      for(let j=t-1; j<i; j++){
        const val = dp[j][t-1] + M[j+1][i] - c;
        if(val > dp[i][t]){
          dp[i][t] = val;
          par[i][t] = j;
        }
      }
    }
  }

  // Reconstruct segments
  const segments = [];
  let curr = n;
  for(let t=k; t>=1; t--){
    const prev = par[curr][t];
    segments.unshift([prev+1, curr]);
    curr = prev;
  }

  return {value: dp[n][k], segments};
}
```

